/*! \mainpage gr-nut

A single, reusable interface between ffmpeg and GNU Radio for analogue
transmission chains: ffmpeg is the codec/format/sync layer, GNU Radio is
the physical layer, and a NUT stream over a pipe/FIFO is the socket
between them.

The module contains one block, gr::nut::nut_source. It ingests a
strict-profile NUT stream (pcm_f32le audio + rawvideo/rgb24 video) and
emits deinterleaved float audio (one port per channel) and rgb24 video
byte streams (one port per stream). The audio sample rate and per-stream
video geometry are adopted from the NUT stream headers at start; the
structure (stream kinds, codecs, channel count) is validated and any
mismatch is a hard error. The flowgraph sink is the only clock — ffmpeg
is paced purely by pipe backpressure.

See the repository README.md for the interface contract, clocking model
and error model, and docs/buffering.md for the buffering and
synchronization reference.

*/
